ronology  but since these are all hosts of the  venom simian i figured we'd go ahead and  discuss them all here anyway kind of  makes the most sense  so after the venom symbiote was  separated from eddie it approached  another of spider-man's perennial foes  the scorpion  matt gargan and so what happens is that  norman osborne had been  imprisoned and needed spider-man to  break him out which of course spider-man  would never do  except that under norman osborne's  orders scorpion had kidnapped aunt may  and would only free her  if spider-man helped break norman out of  jail which makes sense now during the  conversation where mack  explains this arrangement to peter peter  makes the remark that scorpion will  always be  a b-list villain specifically saying  it's not like your venom but when mack  goes home  the venom symbiote is waiting for him  and offers to bond with him telling him  that on his own he'll always be a joke  but if he bonds with a symbiote no one  will ever laugh at him again  obviously scorpion takes him up on this  offer or he wouldn't be in this video  and he becomes venom which granted him  all the same powers that eddie brock had  had as venom until the symbiote was  removed from gargan after he was  arrested for his antics as one of the  dark avengers during the dark brain  story now another of venom's notable  hosts was flash thompson a sometimes  rival and sometimes friend of peter  parker who lost his legs in a heroic  sacrifice during the iraq war now with  the u.s government in possession of the  venom symbiote at the time  and the amazing spider-man number 654 by  dan slott they approached flash about  participating in project rebirth 2.0 now  why do they call it that  because the program that turned steve  rogers into captain america was called  project rebirth and the cardinal rule of  marvel comics is that every organization  without exception  wants to replicate the success of that  original program and create their own  super soldier now flash agrees and is  bonded with the symbiote turning him  into agent venom which grants him all  the powers of his favorite hero  spider-man  as well as venom's shape-shifting  abilities and of specific significance  to flash  the venom symbiote would also allow him  to walk again and he would remain bonded  to the venom symbiote from 2011  up until 2016 and so a pretty long time  by modern comic standards  something else to kind of note here  depending on who you talk to a lot of  people  actually liked agent venom more than  they liked eddie brock venom he was  hugely popular when he first came out  people loved him people loved the story  of asian venom i feel like we should  cover it let me know down in the  comments section if you guys want me to  cover agent venom i don't know if you  guys want me to or not i feel like it'd  be kind of interesting but before we get  into the offspring of the venom symbiote  something that i do want to point out  here is that there are  several more hosts of the venom symbiote  over the years in both the main marvel  continuity and even in alternate  realities for example  in the old man logan universe which  basically imagines the marvel universe  as a desolate post-apocalyptic  wasteland we see the venom symbiote had  actually bonded to a literal t-rex in  wolverine number 69 by mark miller and  steve mcniven now this version seems to  basically be identical to the symbiote  of the 616 universe so we can assume  that this venomous rex venom  venomosaurus rex  this i like venomous rex uh just has the  normal venom powers and abilities  uh on earth 65 the numerical designation  of the universe where gwen stacy became  spider-gwen there is a version of venom  that was created by a scientist named  elsa brock in an attempt to find a cure  for the lizard formula that had turned  that universe's peter parker  into the lizard first appearing in  spider-gwen number 19 by jason letour  and robbie rodriguez the venom of earth  65  is not an alien symbiote but is  artificially created by a reaction  between the radioactive spider isotopes  that gave gwyn her powers and the lizard  formula now gwen would later bond with  the symbiote to become gwynem and  spider-gwen number 24.  the venom symbiote grants its wear all  the powers that spider-gwen had  which are essentially the same as the  spider-man of earth 616 but it also must  have  a compatible host as it will kill  incompatible ones through the radiation  from the spider isotopes furthermore the  symbiote makes its wear subject to  overly aggressive behavior by removing  their inhibitions and amplifying their  emotions and so this version of the  symbiote also retains the weaknesses to  heat and sonics of the main universe  venom now moving on to the offspring of  venom the first and most prominent is of  course  carnage which was created by david  miccolini and mark bagley and first  appeared in amazing spider-man number  361 in 1992. now the carnos symbiote was  created when eddie brock who was bonded  with the venom symbiote at the time  escaped from prison and unbeknownst to  eddie left an offspring behind that  would bond with a cellmate a maniacal  serial killer named cletus cassidy now  cassidy would be the most frequent host  of the carnage symbiote whose abilities  differ significantly from the venom  symbiote because carnage was born into  an environment  alien to its species the environment of  earth and so the carnage symbiote  strength surpasses that of venom  and it also possesses advanced  shape-shifting abilities allowing its  hosts to turn  appendages into weapons and can even  fire projectile weapons made of the  symbiote itself  the symbiote's tendrils can implant  thoughts in the minds of others and can  also relay information it perceives  from any direction to its host  instantaneously the symbiote grants its  host a regenerative healing factor and  like venom is undetectable by peter  parker's spider sense and it